Package: littera
Version: __VERSION__
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: rouhim <rouhim@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: __INSTALLED_SIZE__
Homepage: https://github.com/RouHim/littera
Depends: libc6 (>= __GLIBC__), libgcc-s1, libstdc++6, libasound2t64 | libasound2, libvulkan1, libwayland-client0, libxkbcommon0
Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal, mesa-vulkan-drivers, xdg-utils, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libx11-6, libxcursor1, libxi6, libxrandr2, libxinerama1
Suggests: pipewire-alsa
Description: Local voice dictation for Linux/Wayland
 Littera runs entirely on your machine: press a global hotkey, speak, and
 the transcript is inserted at the cursor of the focused application.
 Recognition runs in-process with a statically linked speech engine
 (Vulkan with a CPU fallback), with no cloud, no account, or separately
 installed speech runtime. The first dictation downloads a SHA-256
 verified speech model (about 751 MB) into the user's XDG data directory.
